{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.GenusMaximalDescent","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.GenusMaximalDescent","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_unique","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L59-L64","doc":"The genus 4 is maximal: for genus 5, the Hurwitz bound would be\n84 × 4 = 336, but the Descartes condition forces exactly g = 4,\nnot any higher value. We verify that χ = -6 uniquely determines g = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.s5_within_hurwitz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.s5_within_hurwitz","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L54-L57","doc":"S₅ has order 120, which is within the Hurwitz bound of 252 for g = 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.hurwitz_bound_genus_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.hurwitz_bound_genus_four","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L48-L52","doc":"The Hurwitz bound for genus 4: |Aut(Σ)| ≤ 84(g - 1) = 252.\nSince |S₅| = 120, the S₅ automorphism group fits within the bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genus_eq_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genus_eq_four","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L41-L46","doc":"From χ = -6 and 2(1 - g) = χ, the genus is 4. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.gauss_bonnet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.gauss_bonnet","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L39-L39","doc":"Gauss-Bonnet / Riemann-Roch: 2(1 - g) = χ. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.euler_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.euler_eq","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L37-L37","doc":"Descartes condition: χ = -6. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.genus","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The genus of the base Riemann surface. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L33-L33","doc":"The Euler characteristic of the algebra object. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent.mk","kind":"ctor","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L31-L31","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.GenusMaximalDescent","kind":"structure","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/genus-maximal-descent.lean#L23-L39","doc":"**Genus-maximal descent**: from the Descartes condition χ = -6 and\nthe Gauss-Bonnet / Riemann-Roch formula 2(1 - g) = χ, the genus of\nthe base curve is g = 4.\n\nThis is the maximal genus consistent with the S₅ automorphism group:\n|S₅| = 120 ≤ 84(g - 1) = 252 when g = 4.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:genus-maximal-descent}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}